{# ===========================================================================
   Components: neon + ftr

   v2 splits what used to be one `.monolith` footer into the two blocks the
   reference file uses: the neon monolith (crest, wordmark, gold rule, slogan)
   sitting directly above a quiet footer (epitaph, spec strip, nav, colophon).

   The markup and data plumbing are almost entirely unchanged. The crest was
   already 但馬 and the wordmark already rendered per-character spans from
   site.shortName via the `chars` filter, which is exactly what .neon__word
   needs. The one genuinely new element is the gold hairline rule.

   WHAT THE REFERENCE DROPS AND THIS KEEPS. _reference/tajima-home-v2.html has
   no epitaph and no spec strip: its footer is a nav and a copyright line. That
   would delete content this footer already publishes, so those blocks move
   into .ftr rather than disappearing.

   Every figure in the spec strip comes from site.json, which traces to
   CLIENT_FACTS.md. Two of them deliberately differ from the reference concept
   and must not be reverted:

     "6 / San Diego"    was "8 Houses". CLIENT_FACTS.md forbids publishing a
                        global location total until the live site's
                        location-count contradiction is fixed.
     "2 / Noodle Types" was "12h Tonkotsu". No simmer time is confirmed
                        anywhere in CLIENT_FACTS.md. That number is invented.

   See the _specNote key in site.json. Do not add a figure without a confirmed
   source.
   =========================================================================== #}

<section class="neon" aria-label="{{ site.name }}">
  <p class="neon__kanji" aria-hidden="true">但馬</p>

  {# Per-letter spans so the wordmark can be styled and animated letter by
     letter. They are aria-hidden and the accessible name comes from the
     aria-label, so a screen reader reads "Tajima" and not six letters. #}
  <p class="neon__word" aria-label="{{ site.shortName }}">
    {%- for letter in site.shortName | upper | chars %}<span class="neon__word-letter" aria-hidden="true">{{ letter }}</span>{% endfor -%}
  </p>

  {# The one sanctioned gradient in the system: transparent to gold to
     transparent. DESIGN_SYSTEM.md bans gradients as a brand device and lists
     this hairline and photo scrims as the only exceptions. #}
  <div class="neon__rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <p class="neon__slogan">
    {{ site.slogan.before }}<em>{{ site.slogan.emphasis }}</em>
  </p>
</section>

<footer class="ftr" aria-label="{{ site.name }} footer">
  <div class="ftr__in">

    <p class="ftr__epitaph">
      {{ site.footer.epitaph.before }}<em>{{ site.footer.epitaph.emphasis }}</em>{{ site.footer.epitaph.after }}
    </p>

    <ul class="ftr__spec" aria-label="{{ site.name }} at a glance">
      {%- for item in site.footer.spec %}
        <li>
          <span class="ftr__spec-num">{{ item.num }}</span>
          <span class="ftr__spec-label">{{ item.label }}</span>
        </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>

    <nav class="ftr__nav" aria-label="Footer">
      {%- for item in nav.footer %}
        {%- set isCurrent = page.url == item.url %}
        <a
          class="ftr__nav-link{% if isCurrent %} ftr__nav-link--current{% endif %}"
          href="{{ item.url }}"
          {%- if item.external %} rel="noopener"{% endif %}
          {%- if isCurrent %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
          {{- item.label }}{% if item.sub %} <span aria-hidden="true">&#8629;</span>{% endif -%}
        </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </nav>

    <div class="ftr__colophon">
      <p class="ftr__sub">
        {{ site.name }} &middot; {{ site.footer.region }} &middot; &copy; {{ buildYear }}
      </p>

      {#
        Theme toggle. Moved here from the header logo, which closes
        DESIGN_SYSTEM.md Open Item 2: the logo is a link home again.

        Light and dark both ship and day is the default. This is a MANUAL
        control: no clock, no prefers-color-scheme.

        Rendered `hidden`. js/theme.js unhides it and sets aria-pressed on
        init. Without JS it would be a control that does nothing, so it should
        not be in the accessibility tree at all. The visible label is the
        accessible name, so nothing overrides it and WCAG 2.5.3 holds; the
        icons carry the current state and are decorative.

        js/theme.js binds to [data-theme-toggle], so this can move again
        without touching the script.
      #}
      <button class="tgl" type="button" data-theme-toggle hidden>
        <svg class="tgl__day" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <circle cx="8" cy="8" r="3.1"/>
          <path d="M8 .9v2.1M8 13v2.1M15.1 8H13M3 8H.9M13 3l-1.5 1.5M4.5 11.5 3 13M13 13l-1.5-1.5M4.5 4.5 3 3"/>
        </svg>
        <svg class="tgl__night" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M13.5 9.9A5.9 5.9 0 0 1 6.1 2.5a5.9 5.9 0 1 0 7.4 7.4Z"/>
        </svg>
        Night mode
      </button>
    </div>

  </div>
</footer>
